l is None:\n2559 |         # Compute classes only if pos_label is not specified:\n2560 |         classes = np.unique(y_true)\n2561 |         if classes.dtype.kind in \"OUS\" or not (\n2562 |             np.array_equal(classes, [0, 1])\n2563 |             or np.array_equal(classes, [-1, 1])\n2564 |             or np.array_equal(classes, [0])\n2565 |             or np.array_equal(classes, [-1])\n2566 |             or np.array_equal(classes, [1])\n2567 |         ):\n2568 |             classes_repr = \", \".join([repr(c) for c in classes.tolist()])\n2569 |             raise ValueError(\n2570 |                 f\"y_true takes value in {{{classes_repr}}} and pos_label is not \"\n2571 |                 \"specified: either make y_true take value in {0, 1} or \"\n2572 |                 \"{-1, 1} or pass pos_label explicitly.\"\n2573 |             )\n2574 |         pos_label = 1\n2575 | \n2576 |     return pos_label\n```\n"}, {"content": "Given the search results and the unique artifacts, it appears that the feature `assert_consistent_docs()` and `_create_args` are most likely related to `sklearn/utils/_testing.py`. Let's focus on this file and search for the exact lines where these functions are defined.\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=file_path_or_pattern>sklearn/utils/_testing.py</parameter>\n<parameter=line_nums>[699, 765]</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\nNo files found for file pattern 'sklearn/utils/_testing.py'. Will search all files.\n...\n"}, {"content": "It seems there is still an issue with finding the file `sklearn/utils/_testing.py`. Let's try a broader search for the file and see if we can locate it correctly.\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=search_terms>\n['_testing.py']\n</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id"